workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) The standard deviations are $\sigma_X=\sqrt{16}=4$ and $\sigma_Y=\sqrt{400}=20$.
$\begin{align*}z_X&=\frac{46-40}{4}\\&=1.5\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}z_Y&=\frac{270-240}{20}\\&=1.5\end{align*}$
Both cutoffs map to $z=1.5$ on the same standard normal curve, so both probabilities equal $P(Z<1.5)$.
